# Nine functions are ever handed in, which is too many for each place to tell apart by comparisons, and each takes and returns a number in a register. A call by value would box the number, the entry of the callee
# would take it out of its box, and so again for the result. The place calls the one function that has the arms for all such places: the double stays in its register on the way in and on the way out.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="apply" role=Source
# CHECK: Double b@[[value]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[result]] = Patchpoint(b@[[value]]:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), {{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK: Double b@[[sum]] = Add(b@[[result]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[sum]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Nothing is boxed, nothing that comes back is tested or converted, and the place does not look at the word of the closure.
# NONE-LABEL: name="apply" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: Reads:AOTSlimClosure_word
# NONE-NOT: pureFunction
# NONE-NOT: IToD(
# NONE-NOT: BitwiseCast(
# NONE-NOT: AboveEqual(
# NONE-LABEL: end of function

# The index may lie outside the list, so the place tests for undefined, and the call of undefined throws where it stands, under the name that is written there.
# IR-LABEL: name="apply"
# IR-NEXT: b0(v0: undefined|f1|f2|f3|f4|f5|f6|f7|f8|f9, v1: number):
# IR-NEXT: [[isNoFunction]]: boolean = TypeTest v0 testedType=undefined|null
# IR-NEXT: TestAndBranch [[isNoFunction]] -> taken [[throws]](), notTaken [[calls]](| 0)
# IR-NEXT: [[throws]]() frequency=Rare:
# IR: : never = Call {{*}}, -, v1 calleeName="operation"
# IR: [[calls]]([[function]]: f1|f2|f3|f4|f5|f6|f7|f8|f9):
# IR-NEXT: [[result]]: number = CallDirect [[function]], v1 function={{*}}[isNeverInlined]
# The shared function takes any function and expects the nine: a closure that has got a property or another name since it was made passes no test, and is called as a value behind the arms. No stack trace lists it.
# IR-LABEL: name="callWithSharedArms" module=- role=OutlinedBody length=2 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=function}, {type=number}] results=[{type=number}]
# IR-NEXT: b0(v0: function, v1: number):
# IR-COUNT-9: : boolean = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=f
# IR: ([[other]]: function) frequency=Unlikely:
# IR-NEXT: [[boxed]]: anything = Call [[other]], -, v1
# IR-NEXT: : number = AssumeType [[boxed]] provenType=number

# The nine tests are of one word for nine constants: the word of the closure is loaded once, and an entry of a jump table leads to the arm.
# SHARED-LABEL: name="callWithSharedArms" role=OutlinedBody
# SHARED: Int64 b@[[closure]] = ArgumentReg(
# SHARED-NEXT: Int32 b@[[word]] = Load(b@[[closure]], offset = 12, ControlDependent|Reads:AOTSlimClosure_word,
# SHARED: Int32 b@[[index]] = Add(b@[[word]],
# SHARED: Void b@{{*}} = Patchpoint<CloningForbidden>(b@{{*}}:SomeRegister, runsWithoutFrame, resultConstraints = WarmAny, Terminal,
# SHARED-NEXT: Successors: #{{*}}, #{{*}}, #{{*}}, #{{*}}, #{{*}}, #{{*}}, #{{*}}, #{{*}}, #{{*}}, Unlikely:#
# SHARED-LABEL: end of function
# ONCE-LABEL: name="callWithSharedArms" role=OutlinedBody
# ONCE: Reads:AOTSlimClosure_word
# ONCE-NOT: Reads:AOTSlimClosure_word
# ONCE-NOT: = Equal(
# ONCE-LABEL: end of function
